\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Per-task top-1 accuracy on the eight-task CLIP suite: zero-shot backbone, task expert, task-arithmetic merge, and the proposed gated refinement (APR, $\eta =8$). Refinement recovers most of the merge's interference loss, including on Cars and SUN397, which the merge had degraded below the zero-shot backbone.}}{14}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:clip8pt}{{4}{14}{Per-task top-1 accuracy on the eight-task CLIP suite: zero-shot backbone, task expert, task-arithmetic merge, and the proposed gated refinement (APR, $\eta =8$). Refinement recovers most of the merge's interference loss, including on Cars and SUN397, which the merge had degraded below the zero-shot backbone}{table.4}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Replay-budget study on the eight-task CLIP suite (mean normalized retention; worst-task in parentheses). Best configuration per family; the gated update (APR) near-converges by $S=5\text  {--}10$ sweeps, while ordinary replay GD is given a longer horizon ($S=25\text  {--}35$) as a generous baseline. APR holds an ${\approx }\,+0.10$ mean advantage at every budget and is the only method with non-negative worst-task retention down to $n=16$.}}{14}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:clipbudget}{{5}{14}{Replay-budget study on the eight-task CLIP suite (mean normalized retention; worst-task in parentheses). Best configuration per family; the gated update (APR) near-converges by $S=5\text {--}10$ sweeps, while ordinary replay GD is given a longer horizon ($S=25\text {--}35$) as a generous baseline. APR holds an ${\approx }\,+0.10$ mean advantage at every budget and is the only method with non-negative worst-task retention down to $n=16$}{table.5}{}}
